    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d714">

                <pb facs="0837" n="551" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg551"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 165.102/809</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-21T13:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 21, 1916, 1 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2759. Your 3586, January 15, 3 p. m. Due to great increase in value dyestuffs,
                    impossible state value, but estimated two cargoes, which is quantity desired,
                    about $5,000,000. Urge early action and cable specifically <hi
                        rendition="#italic">re</hi> sugar-beet seed, cyanide, and porcelain
                    guides.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
